.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-storage-set-content - Ensure a storage's content list includes a content type, idempotently


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge storage set-content <target-id> <storage> <content-type> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Ensure a storage's cluster-wide content list includes <content-type>
(one of: images, rootdir, iso, vztmpl, backup, snippets, import) — an add-only
toggle.

.PP
Idempotent: already present -> no-op; absent -> added, preserving the storage's
existing content types and re-sorting the list. The write is a compare-and-swap
on PVE's own config digest (PUT /storage/{name}), so a concurrent change to the
same storage is detected and the write retried rather than clobbering it.

.PP
set-content does NOT create a storage (it errors if the storage does not exist)
and does NOT remove a content type.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	re-run the write even when the content type is already present

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set-content

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-storage(1)\fP
